    "title": "Spurs' Playoff Run Ends in First Round",
    "text": "• The San Antonio Spurs lost their first playoff series since 2019.\n• The Spurs lost to the Denver Nuggets in five games.\n• The Nuggets won the series 4-1.\n• The Spurs' lack of playoff experience was not a major factor.\n• Dejounte Murray scored 26 points in Game 4.\n• Keldon Johnson, Devin Vassell, and Tre Jones also had strong performances.\n• The Spurs averaged 100.6 points per game, while the Nuggets averaged 110.6.\n• The Spurs were outscored by the Nuggets 530-488 in the series.\n• The Spurs' season ended after losing Game 5 on April 28.\n• The Spurs were outscored in the series by a total of 42 points.\n• The Spurs were swept in the series by the Nuggets.\n• The Spurs were eliminated from the playoffs by the Nuggets.",
